---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import Code from "../../components/Code.astro";
const handle = "<returned task_handle>";
---

<Docs
  title="Native tasks"
  description="Delegate work in a specific project, inspect its state, and continue the same private CLI session when supported."
  toc={[
    ["start", "Start and poll"],
    ["followup", "Follow up or cancel"],
    ["ownership", "Redelivery and ownership"],
    ["retention", "Retention and limits"],
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="start">Start and poll</h2>
  <p>
    Call the MCP tool <code>clink</code> with <code>action: "start"</code>.
    Choose an admitted native agent and an existing project inside its approved
    roots. The CLI can use its native tools and integrations. See{" "}
    <a href="/reference/#admissions">which builds support this operation</a>.
  </p>
  <Code
    label="MCP · clink · start"
    code={JSON.stringify(
      {
        action: "start",
        cli_name: "claude",
        project_dir: "/absolute/path/to/your-project",
        request_key: "parser-tests-start-1",
        prompt: "Run the existing parser tests and report the failures.",
        timeout_seconds: 180,
      },
      null,
      2,
    )}
  />
  <p>
    A start response schedules an attempt. Save its <code>task_handle</code> and
    poll for a terminal state. A completed response records successful terminal
    execution. Inspect the output and verify the actual effects in the project.
  </p>
  <Code
    label="MCP · clink · status"
    code={JSON.stringify({ action: "status", task_handle: handle }, null, 2)}
  />
  <h2 id="followup">Follow up or cancel</h2>
  <p>
    When <code>followup_available</code> is true, send only the new input with a
    fresh key. The new attempt keeps the original agent, project, role,
    instructions and model selection.
  </p>
  <Code
    label="MCP · clink · followup"
    code={JSON.stringify(
      {
        action: "followup",
        task_handle: handle,
        request_key: "parser-tests-followup-1",
        prompt: "Explain the first failure and cite the relevant test.",
      },
      null,
      2,
    )}
  />
  <Code
    label="MCP · clink · cancel"
    code={JSON.stringify({ action: "cancel", task_handle: handle }, null, 2)}
  />
  <p>
    Cancellation is idempotent and triggers local cleanup. Earlier filesystem or
    external changes can persist. A native permission refusal may return{" "}
    <code>permission_needed</code>. Examine it using the CLI’s normal trust and
    permission controls.
  </p>
  <h2 id="ownership">Redelivery and ownership</h2>
  <p>
    Give each intended start or follow-up a unique <code>request_key</code> of
    1–128 ASCII characters. Start with a letter or digit. The remaining
    characters may also include <code>_ . : -</code>. If the response is lost,
    redeliver the same key and identical arguments while the server still holds
    the task. Changed inputs return <code>request_key_conflict</code>. After a
    restart, inspect real effects before submitting again.
  </p>
  <p>
    One active native writer can own a canonical project and its overlapping
    parents or children. This coordination covers tasks in that server process.
    Work started outside it can still modify the project.
  </p>
  <h2 id="retention">Retention and limits</h2>
  <p>
    The server retains up to 64 tasks, 16 attempts per task and 8 MiB of task
    data. Only the latest result is retained, up to 20,000 characters. Inactive
    terminal records expire after three hours. Polling does not extend
    retention. Restart discards handles, mappings and deduplication records.
  </p>
  <p>
    By default the pool runs two CLI processes and admits eight waiters. Queue
    wait is capped at 30 seconds and each attempt at 1,800 seconds including
    preparation and queueing. Set a shorter <code>timeout_seconds</code> when
    appropriate.
  </p>
</Docs>
